hadiths[63]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2796","It was narrated to us by Maḥmūd ibn Ghaylān, who narrated to us from Abū Dāwūd, who narrated to us from Shuʿbah, from Abū Isḥāq, from al-Barāʾ — though he did not hear it directly from him — that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, passed by a group of the Anṣār sitting in the road, and he said:\n\n\If you must do this"," then return the greeting of peace"," assist the oppressed"," and guide the way.\""\n\nIn this chapter"," there are narrations from Abū Hurayrah and Abū Shurayḥ al-Khuzāʿī.\n\nAbū ʿĪsā said: This is a ḥasan gharīb hadith."""
"2797","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \The thigh is 'Awrah"""
"2798","Narrated Abu Az-Zinad:\Ibn Jarhad informed me from his father"""
"2799","Narrated Salih bin Abi Hassan:\I heard Sa'eed bin Musayyab saying: 'Indeed Allah is Tayyib (good) and he loves Tayyib (what is good)"""
"2800","**Narrated by Ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet ﷺ, who said:**\n\n**\Part of the completeness of the greeting (at-taḥiyyah) is the taking of the hand (i.e."""","""" shaking hands).\""""""""**\n\n**In this chapter"""","""" there are narrations from al-Barāʾ and Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them).**\n\n**Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said:** This is a *gharīb* (uncommon) hadith"""","""" and we do not know it except through the narration of Yaḥyā ibn Sulaym from Sufyān.\n\n**He said:** I asked Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl (al-Bukhārī) about this hadith"""","""" and he did not consider it to be *maḥfūẓ* (reliably preserved). He said: \""""""""In my view"""","""" what was actually intended is the hadith of Sufyān from Manṣūr"""","""" from Khaythamah"""","""" from one who heard Ibn Masʿūd narrate from the Prophet ﷺ"""","""" who said: **'There should be no late-night conversation (samar) except for one who is praying or a traveller.'**\""""""""\n\n**Muḥammad (al-Bukhārī) said:** Rather"""","""" it is narrated from Manṣūr"""","""" from Abū Isḥāq"""","""" from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd or someone else"""","""" who said: **\""""""""Part of the completeness of the greeting is the taking of the hand.\""""""""**\n\n*Note: This narration is classified as gharīb by Imam al-Tirmidhī"""","""" and Imam al-Bukhārī expressed reservations regarding its chain of transmission"""","""" suggesting a possible confusion in the isnād.*"""""""""
"2801","Narrated Jabir:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day"""
"2802","Narrated Abu 'Udhrah [and he lived during the time of the Prophet (ﷺ)]:from 'Aishah"
"2803","Narrated Abu Al-Malih Al-Hudhali:that some women from the inhabitants of Hims, or from the inhabitants of Ash-Sham entered upon 'Aishah, so she said: ""Are you those whose women enter the Hammamat? I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: 'No woman removes her garments in other than the house of her husband except that she has torn the screen between herself and her Lord"
"2804","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\I heard Abu Talhah saying: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: \""The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an object of images"""
"2805","Narrated Ishaq bin 'Abdullah bin Abi Talhah:that Rafi' bin Ishaq informed him, saying: ""I and 'Abdullah bin Abi Talhah entered upon Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri to visit him. So Abu Sa'eed said: 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) informed us: ""The angels do not enter a house in which there is an image or a picture"
"2806","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amr:\A man passed by while wearing two red garments. He gave Salam to the Prophet (ﷺ) but he did not return the Salam"""
"2807","Narrated 'Ali bin Abi Talib:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited the gold ring"""
"2808","Narrated Al-Bara bin 'Azib:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered us with seven things and he forbade us from seven. He ordered us to follow the funeral"""
"2809","Narrated Samurah bin Jundab:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Wear white"""
"2810","Narrated Samurah bin Jundab:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Wear white, for indeed it is very pure and cleaner, and shroud your dead in it"
"2811","Narrated Abu Rimthah:\I saw the Messenger of Allah wearing two green Burud"""
"2812","Narrated 'Aishah:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went out during the morning wearing a Mirt made of black hair"""
"2813","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Hassan:that his grandmothers Safiyyah bint 'Ulaibah and Dhuhaibah bint 'Ulaibah narrated to him"
"2814","Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited saffron for men"
"2815","Narrated Ya'la bin Murrah:\The Prophet (ﷺ) saw a man wearing Khuluq and said: 'Go and wash it"""
"2816","Narrated The freed slave of Asma:from Ibn 'Umar who said: \I heard 'Umar mentioning that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'Whoever wears silk in the world he shall not wear it in the Hereafter"""
"2817","Narrated Al-Miswar bin Makhramah:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) distributed some cloaks but he did not give anything to Makhramah. Makhramah said: 'O my son! Let us go to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).' So I went with him. He said: 'Enter and call him for me.'So I called the Prophet (ﷺ) for him"""
"2818","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated from Ikrimah ibn Ammar a narration similar to that of Ibn al-Mubarak, and in the third instance he said to him: \You are afflicted with illness (mazkum).\"" Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated this to us"," who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated it to us."""
"2819","Narrated Ibn Buraidah:from his father: \An-Najashi gave the Prophet (ﷺ) two black plain Khuff. So he wore them"""
"2820","It was narrated to us by Muhammad ibn Wazir al-Wasiti, it was narrated to us by Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Muhammad ibn 'Ajlan, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah that when the Prophet ﷺ sneezed, he would cover his face with his hand or with his garment, thereby muffling his voice with it. Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: This is a hasan sahih hadith."
"2821","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The one whose counsel is sought is entrusted"""
"2822","Narrated Umm Salamah:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'The one whose council is sought is entrusted"""
"2823","**Narrated by 'Adiyy ibn Thābit, from his father, from his grandfather, who reported it in a *marfū'* (elevated) narration, that he (the Prophet ﷺ) said:**\n\n> **\Sneezing"""","""" drowsiness"""","""" and yawning during the prayer"""","""" as well as menstruation"""","""" vomiting"""","""" and nosebleeds"""","""" are from the Shayṭān (Satan).\""""""""**\n\n**Abū 'Īsā (al-Tirmidhī) said:** \""""""""This is a *gharīb* (uncommon/singular) hadith. We do not know it except through the narration of Sharīk from Abū al-Yaqẓān.\""""""""\n\n**He further said:** \""""""""I asked Muḥammad ibn Ismā'īl (al-Bukhārī) about 'Adiyy ibn Thābit"""","""" from his father"""","""" from his grandfather. I asked him: 'What is the name of 'Adiyy's grandfather?' He said: 'I do not know.'\""""""""\n\n**It has been mentioned on the authority of Yaḥyya ibn Ma'īn that he said:** \""""""""His name is Dīnār.\""""""""\n\n- **"""""""""
"2824","Narrated 'Abdullah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whenever there are three of you"""
"2825","Narrated Isma'il bin Abi Khalid:that Abu Juhaifah said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) (he was) white and turning grey. Al-Hasan bin 'Ali resembles him most. He had promised thirteen young she-camels for us"""
"2826","Narrated Isma'il bin Abi Khalid:that Abu Juhaifah said: \I saw the Prophet (ﷺ)"""
"2827","Narrated 'Ali:\I did not hear the Prophet (ﷺ) mentioning both of his parents (that is including both in the saying \""May my father and mother be ransomed for you\"") for anyone other than Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas"""
"2828","Narrated 'Ali:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not mention both of his parents for anyone except Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas. On the Day of Uhud he said: 'Shoot"""
"2829","Narrated Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) mentioned both of his parents to me on the Day of Uhud"""
"2830","Narrated Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) mentioned both of his parents to me on the Day of Uhud"
"2831","Narrated by al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥulwānī al-Khallāl and others, who said: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us, Maʿmar informed us, from al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Five are from the natural disposition (fiṭrah): shaving the pubic hair"," circumcision"," trimming the moustache"," plucking the armpit hair"," and clipping the nails.\"" Abū ʿĪsā said: This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ hadith."""
"2832","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \The most loved names to Allah are 'Abdullah and 'Abdur-Rahman"""
"2833","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \The most loved names to Allah are 'Abdullah and 'Abdur-Rahman"""
"2834","Narrated 'Umar [bin Al-Khattab]:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I forbid naming with Rafi"""
"2835","Narrated Samurah bin Jundab:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Do not name your boy Rabah"""
"2836","Narrated Al-A'raj:that Abu Hurairah conveyed to him that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \The most despicable (Akhna) name to Allah on the Day of Judgement is that of a man named King of Kings. (Malikil-Amlak)"""
"2837","Narrated Al-A'raj:that Abu Hurairah conveyed to him that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""The most despicable (Akhna) name to Allah on the Day of Judgement is that of a man named King of Kings. (Malikil-Amlak)"
"2838","Narrated 'Aishah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) would change abhorrent names"
"2839","Narrated Muhammad bin Jubair bin Mut'im:from his father that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I have some names: I am Muhammad"""
"2840","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) prohibited that one use his name and his Kunyah; naming themselves Muhammad Abul-Qasim"
"2841","Narrated Jabir:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): \When you name yourself after me"""
"2842","Narrated 'Ali bin Abi Talib:that he said: \O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)! If I have a son after you do you think I could name him your Kunyah?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" So he said: \""So that was permitted for me"""
"2843","Narrated 'Abdullah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed some poetry is wisdom"""
"2844","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed some poetry is wisdom"""
"2845","Narrated 'Aishah:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had a Minbar placed in the Masjid for Hassan to stand to boast (poetically) about the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)\"" - or she said: \""to defend the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). And the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Indeed Allah has aided Hassan with the holy spirit (Jibril) as he boasts about - or - defends the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"""
"2846","Narrated Anas:that the Prophet (ﷺ) entered Makkah during 'Umratil-Qada and 'Abdullah bin Rawahah was walking in front of him reciting verses of poetry. \O tribes of disbelievers get out of his way - today we will strike you about its revelation; a strike that removes the heads from the shoulders - and makes the friend not concerned about his friend.\"" 'Umar said to him: \""O Ibn Rawahah! Before the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"""
"2847","Narrated by Abū Masʿūd (may Allāh be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \n\A man should not be led in prayer in his domain"," nor should anyone be seated in his place of honor in his house"," except with his permission.\"" \n\nAbū ʿĪsā (may Allāh have mercy on him) said: This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ hadith."""
"2848","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \The best statement spoken by the Arab is the saying of Labid: 'Everything aside from Allah perishes"""
"2849","Narrated Jabir bin Samurah:\I sat with the Prophet (ﷺ) more than one-hundred times. His Companions used to recite poetry and talk about things that occurred during Jahiliyyah"""
"2850","Narrated Muhammad bin Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas:from his father that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \It is better that one of you fill his insides with puss than to fill it with poetry"""
"2851","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \It is better that one of you fill his insides with puss than to fill it with poetry"""
"2852","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amr:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed Allah detests the excessive among men"""
"2853","Narrated Jabir:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited that a man sleep on a terrace without something to obstruct him (so that he will not roll off and fall)"""
"2854","Narrated 'Abdullah:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to take care of us by preaching during the days fearing that we may get bored"""
"2855","Narrated Abu Salih:\I asked 'Aishah and Umm Salamah about which deed did the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) like to do most. They said: 'Whatever he could do regularly"""
"2856","Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Cover the vessels"""
"2857","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When you travel through fertile land"""
"2858","Narrated An-Nawwas bin Sam'an Al-Kilabi:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed Allah has made a parable of the straight path: At the sides of the path there are walls with open doors"""
